NUM-36: send the groundwater volume the aquifer released, not a trapezoid

GWSolver::execute() integrates the aquifer ODE over the runoff step but keeps
only the end-of-step GW flow rate; routing interpolates between the previous
and the new end-of-step rate (from 0 on the first step) and the mass balance
books their trapezoid, which differs from the volume that left the aquifer
(+13.7 % with a 1-day DRY_STEP). Integrate the outflow volume as a third ODE
component, store its step-average rate as both the old and the new GW flow,
and make the engine's interpolation start from the same rate, as
NUM-36_swmm530.patch does for 5.3.0.

The third variable is the total aquifer depth minus the outflow volume, so
the solver's relative error test holds it to the accuracy of the zone
depths; a variable starting at 0 would make the solver give up where GW
flow begins.

Requires: IO-46

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-36_swmm600.patch

